/**
@mainpage LPTA — LLVM Pass Transformation Analysis

@section about What this tool is

LPTA runs LLVM's optimization pipeline on an IR file (.ll) while
instrumenting every pass via PassInstrumentationCallbacks. For each pass
execution it records the state of the IR before and after, computes
structural deltas (instructions, blocks, calls, branches, ...), optionally
saves IR snapshots for passes that changed something, measures codegen size
with llc, and emits history.json — visualized by an interactive dashboard.

@section pipeline The data pipeline at a glance

@verbatim
  input.ll ──parseIRFile──▶ Module
                               │
              PassBuilder + PassInstrumentationCallbacks
                               │
      BEFORE callback ──push──▶ PassFrame stack          g_events ◀── push
                               │                             │
                           pass runs                         │
                               │                             │
      AFTER / INVALIDATED ─pop─┘                    writeHistoryJSON()
                                                             │
  ir_before_opt.ll / ir_after_opt.ll ──llc──▶ asm sizes   history.json
                                                             │
                                              python -m http.server
                                                             │
                                                      Dashboard (fetch)
@endverbatim

@section docs More documentation

- @subpage arch_data_flow — runtime data-flow diagrams (Mermaid source in docs/architecture/)
- @subpage arch_project_map — annotated repository map

@section layers Proving the numbers right (7 layers)

1. Hand-countable ground truth (tests/tiny_proof.ll)
2. Independent grep-based recounting (tests/validate_correctness.sh)
3. LLVM opt -stats cross-validation
4. Byte-identical determinism across runs
5. Runtime assert() counting invariants
6. Unit tests (build/test_utilities.exe)
7. Mutation fuzzing (300+ inputs)

@page arch_data_flow Data Flow Diagrams
The Mermaid sources live in docs/architecture/DATA_FLOW.md and are rendered
nicely by GitHub, VS Code (Mermaid extension), or docs/architecture/index.html.

@page arch_project_map Project Map
See docs/architecture/PROJECT_MAP.md for the annotated repository tree.
*/
